{"date": "2026-10-11", "title": "Public Sector Workers Plan Strike Over Pay", "level": "B2", "summaryZh": "超過十萬名愛爾蘭公部門員工因薪資爭議，預計於10月14日罷工。", "sources": [{"name": "The Irish Times", "url": "https://www.irishtimes.com/politics/2026/10/11/who-is-affected-by-next-weeks-strike-and-can-it-be-averted-in-a-last-minute-deal/"}], "paragraphs": ["More than 100,000 public sector workers in Ireland are preparing to go on strike this Wednesday, 14 October, in a dispute over pay. Teachers, nurses, doctors and school support staff are all expected to take part, and further stoppages are planned for 21 October.", "Several large trade unions are involved, including Fórsa, Siptu and the Irish Nurses and Midwives Organisation. For the first time, dentists working for the Health Service Executive (HSE) will also join the action.", "The last public service pay agreement expired in June. The unions argue that wages have not kept up with inflation, and they accuse the Government of attaching conditions before talks can even begin.", "The impact on daily life could be significant. Most schools may close, which means many working parents will have to take a day off or find someone to look after their children. In the health service, up to 150,000 medical appointments could be cancelled, although emergency care is expected to continue as normal.", "The Minister for Public Expenditure, Jack Chambers, says an agreement could already have been reached. He claims the unions walked away after only two meetings, and he wants any new deal to include public service reform. In the recent budget, the Government set aside €1.2 billion for pay increases, but the unions say this is far from enough.", "Experts in industrial relations believe a compromise is still possible. However, they warn that both sides need to act quickly if they want to avoid disruption next week."], "gloss": {"a": {"zh": "一個", "pos": "art.", "base": "a"}, "accuse": {"zh": "指控；指責", "pos": "v.", "base": "accuse", "note": {"meaning": "指控某人做了錯事。", "usage": "固定搭配 accuse someone OF doing something，介系詞用 of，不是 for。", "collocations": ["accuse sb of", "be accused of", "falsely accused"], "example": {"en": "She accused him of lying.", "zh": "她指控他說謊。"}}}, "act": {"zh": "採取行動", "pos": "v.", "base": "act"}, "action": {"zh": "行動（此指罷工行動）", "pos": "n.", "base": "action"}, "after": {"zh": "在…之後", "pos": "prep.", "base": "after"}, "agreement": {"zh": "協議", "pos": "n.", "base": "agreement"}, "all": {"zh": "全部；都", "pos": "det.", "base": "all"}, "already": {"zh": "已經", "pos": "adv.", "base": "already"}, "also": {"zh": "也", "pos": "adv.", "base": "also"}, "although": {"zh": "雖然；儘管", "pos": "conj.", "base": "although"}, "an": {"zh": "一個", "pos": "art.", "base": "an"}, "and": {"zh": "和；而且", "pos": "conj.", "base": "and"}, "any": {"zh": "任何", "pos": "det.", "base": "any"}, "appointments": {"zh": "（醫療）預約；門診", "pos": "n.", "base": "appointment"}, "are": {"zh": "是", "pos": "v.", "base": "be"}, "argue": {"zh": "主張；爭辯", "pos": "v.", "base": "argue"}, "as": {"zh": "如同；作為", "pos": "prep.", "base": "as"}, "aside": {"zh": "在一旁（set aside：撥出、預留）", "pos": "adv.", "base": "aside"}, "attaching": {"zh": "附加（條件）", "pos": "v.", "base": "attach", "note": {"meaning": "附加、附上；這裡指談判前「附加條件」。", "usage": "attach A to B；attach conditions to something 是新聞常見說法。", "collocations": ["attach conditions", "attach a file", "strings attached"], "example": {"en": "The loan comes with no strings attached.", "zh": "這筆貸款沒有附帶任何條件。"}}}, "avoid": {"zh": "避免", "pos": "v.", "base": "avoid"}, "away": {"zh": "離開", "pos": "adv.", "base": "away"}, "be": {"zh": "是", "pos": "v.", "base": "be"}, "been": {"zh": "是（be 的過去分詞）", "pos": "v.", "base": "be"}, "before": {"zh": "在…之前", "pos": "conj.", "base": "before"}, "begin": {"zh": "開始", "pos": "v.", "base": "begin"}, "believe": {"zh": "相信；認為", "pos": "v.", "base": "believe"}, "billion": {"zh": "十億", "pos": "n.", "base": "billion"}, "both": {"zh": "雙方；兩者都", "pos": "det.", "base": "both"}, "budget": {"zh": "（政府）預算", "pos": "